VecApp

A unified and simplified system for purposeful discipleship in the church.

Overview

VecApp is a web and mobile platform designed to help churches nurture, track, and grow disciples with structure and purpose. It brings together mentorship, training, and accountability, all in one place.

Why It Matters

Many churches struggle with fragmented or manual discipleship processes, losing track of members’ spiritual growth, mentorship activities, and follow-ups.  
DiscipleHub solves this by offering a centralized digital system that enables pastors and leaders to guide believers from members → mature disciples → servant leaders.

Who It’s For
Pastors: to monitor and manage discipleship progress across the church.  
Leaders/Mentors: to communicate, assign lessons, and track mentees’ spiritual journeys.  
Members/Disciples: to grow with structured teachings, accountability, and community support.

Key Features

Digital Curriculum: interactive discipleship lessons and growth modules.  
Progress Tracker: visualize spiritual growth and completion levels.  
Mentor Dashboard: assign, track, and communicate with disciples.  
Reminders & Notifications: for prayer times, lessons, and follow-ups.  
Community Chat: small group engagement and encouragement.  
Analytics Reports: insights on growth, engagement, and group health.  

Technologies (Planned Stack)

| Layer | Technology | Purpose |
|-------|-------------|----------|
| Frontend | React (Web) / Flutter (Mobile) | User interfaces |
| Backend | Node.js (Express) / Django | APIs & business logic |
| Database | PostgreSQL / Firebase | Data storage |
| Authentication | Firebase Auth / JWT | Secure user access |
| Hosting | AWS / Vercel / Firebase Hosting | Deployment & scalability |

Project Vision

VecApp’s goal is to make discipleship **structured, measurable, and relational, empowering churches worldwide to disciple effectively through technology.

Roadmap (MVP Focus)

1. Build user authentication (Pastor / Leader / Disciple).  
2. Create core discipleship tracker and progress dashboard.  
3. Enable content upload and viewing (lessons, teachings).  
4. Add notifications and group chat.  
5. Pilot test with 5–10 churches.  



